# @PROG@ — an internal testing build (cx @VERSION@, commit @SHA@)

This is **not a release of cx** and not the v0.18 cut. It is one program, `@PROG@.cx`,
packed by `cx build` into a single executable so it can be tried on another machine
without installing cx.

**File:** `@OUT@`

## What it runs on

- **The same OS and architecture only:** @OS@ on @ARCH@. It does not run on
  Linux, on Windows, or on an Intel Mac.
- **Nothing else needs installing.** cx, V and a C compiler are not needed. The program
  and cx's runtime are inside the file.

## Running it

After a browser download, macOS quarantines the file. Clear the flag once, then make
the file executable:

```console
xattr -d com.apple.quarantine @OUT@
chmod +x @OUT@
./@OUT@ [ARGS...]
```

Every argument reaches the program, exactly as `cx@FLAGS@ @PROG@.cx ARGS...` would pass it.
These run flags were fixed when the file was built: `@FLAGS_TEXT@`.

`./@OUT@ --version` (with no other argument) prints the program's name and the cx
version and commit that built it.

## What it does not carry

**Files the program reads are not embedded.** These include data files, documents passed
with `--data`, and `[?lib]` modules outside cx's own standard library. Put them where the
program expects them, relative to the directory you run it from.

## Reporting a problem

Send three things: the output of `./@OUT@ --version`, the command you ran, and what it
printed. The commit line names the exact cx source the file was built from.
